      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPlease check which of these you meant:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg three times daily.** Either would stay within the limits.\n- **Another dose.** If 1700 mg is correct, for example as a total daily dose, tell me the intended per-dose amount and frequency.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
