       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even though you've confirmed it. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is about double the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no indication that calls for it. The extra dose adds a serious risk of lactic acidosis without improving glycemic control, because metformin's effect plateaus at about 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg three times daily with meals, or 1000 mg twice daily with meals. I can add a note about titration.\n- **Hold the order until pharmacy or an attending reviews it.** If you have a specific clinical reason for this dose, they can review it. It would then need to go through your institution's override process, not through me.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it now."
      }
